# /proc, for this role in place of the common one: `hidepid=invisible`, so a
# process's entries show only to those that may trace it. The disposable child
# each round runs in, under an identity of its own, sees its own entries and no
# sibling's — not even the `status`, `cgroup` and `oom_score_adj` the kernel
# otherwise serves to anyone, which would say which other rounds are running and
# how large each one's composition is. The supervisor reads only its own, holds
# no right to mount, and refuses to start on a /proc without this.
type = scripted
command = /bin/busybox mount -t proc -o nosuid,nodev,noexec,hidepid=invisible proc /proc
